lg-thinq-specialty-cycles
=========================

This project is an independent, unofficial Python client for LG ThinQ2 laundry
devices. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or partnered with LG
Electronics.

The protocol knowledge in this repository was learned from public community
work. This library is not first, and it does not replace those projects.


Prior art (please use and credit these)
---------------------------------------

1. ollo69 / ha-smartthinq-sensors
   https://github.com/ollo69/ha-smartthinq-sensors
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Copyright: ollo69 and contributors

   This is the primary source for ThinQ2 laundry remote-start payloads,
   CourseType.COURSE vs CourseType.SMARTCOURSE, model-info course catalogs,
   and WMStart / control-sync command shape. Specialty (download) cycles
   live in the SmartCourse catalog on many washers and dryers; UI lists that
   only load CourseType.COURSE omit them.

2. sampsyo / wideq
   https://github.com/sampsyo/wideq
   License: MIT
   Copyright (c) 2018 Adrian Sampson

   Original reverse-engineered ThinQ client: gateway discovery, EMP OAuth,
   refresh-token signing, and the overall unofficial API approach.

3. tinkerborg / thinq2-python
   https://github.com/tinkerborg/thinq2-python
   License: GNU General Public License v3.0

   Early ThinQ2 HTTP client and control-sync documentation. This repository
   does not copy or distribute that project's source. It is listed here as
   prior art only.


